Answer: According to the source, the primary cause of death for most victims ofthe 1918 influenza pandemic was **bacterial pneumonia** that developed after initial flu infections, not the influenza virus itself. As the article states, "bacterial pneumonia that came on the heels of mostly mild cases of flu killed the majority of the 20 to 100 million victims of the so-called Spanish flu," and Anthony Fauci himself agreed, saying, "We agree completely that bacterial pneumonia played a major role in the mortality of the 1918 pandemic." The source attributes the bacterial infections to the flu virus damaging respiratory tract cells and weakening the immune system — **not to face masks** as the claim suggests.

Source URL: https://www.newscientist.com/article/dn14458-bacteria-were-the-real-killers-in-1918-flu-pandemic/

